From 9686757d6fc37529e76bb8010f84e02786432133 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ryoma-89 <ryoma-89@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:41:52 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] util/perf: compile trace scopes out when no trace backend is
 enabled

MESA_TRACE_SCOPE expanded to a scope object whenever the compiler supports
the cleanup attribute, even with perfetto, gpuvis and sysprof all disabled.
Each entry then formatted the scope name with vsnprintf into a 4 KiB stack
buffer that nothing consumed. The gfxstream guest uses scopes in its
transport polling loops; in a draw-heavy Vulkan benchmark the formatting
took about a third of the guest CPU time. Require a backend for the scope
implementation; otherwise the macros expand to nothing, as they already do
for compilers without the cleanup attribute.

On WHPX with the ASG transport (vk-render, 20000 draws per frame): 485 ->
771 frames/s, guest CPU per frame 1.30 -> 0.52 ms, identical image checksums.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Generated-by: LLM
Marker required by the Mesa AGENTS.md for generated prose: biblioklept

Change-Id: I452eedee63dd2efb62e075a21801e72d39d7b575
---
 src/util/perf/cpu_trace.h | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/util/perf/cpu_trace.h b/src/util/perf/cpu_trace.h
index 60c0382..28a2824 100644
--- a/src/util/perf/cpu_trace.h
+++ b/src/util/perf/cpu_trace.h
@@ -95,7 +95,10 @@ struct mesa_trace_flow {
 
 #endif /* HAVE_SYSPROF */
 
-#if __has_attribute(cleanup) && __has_attribute(unused)
+/* Without a trace backend, a scope would still format its name with vsnprintf
+ * into a 4 KiB stack buffer on every entry; gfxstream uses scopes in its
+ * transport polling loops. */
+#if __has_attribute(cleanup) && __has_attribute(unused) &&    (defined(HAVE_PERFETTO) || defined(HAVE_GPUVIS) || defined(HAVE_SYSPROF))
 
 #include <stdarg.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
